# Copy to .env (git-ignored) for local runs: `cp .env.example .env`, then fill in values. Never commit .env.
# The live server does NOT read this file: add the same names as GitHub encrypted secrets on
# Recourse-Software-Inc/knowbot (environment "github-pages"); the deploy workflow passes them to the Worker.

# KnowBot Studio Builder (Claude Haiku 5.5)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
KNOWBOT_STUDIO_PROVIDER=anthropic
KNOWBOT_STUDIO_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# knowDrive store the bots answer from (local runs against a real store only)
KNOWDRIVE_API_KEY=

# Phone channel (Twilio Voice) and SMS. Each is optional; a feature without its secret stays off ("not configured").
# Twilio: signs every webhook (TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN); the account SID lets the phone agent hang up and text links.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# The Twilio number product-link texts are sent from (E.164, e.g. +15551234567).
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
# KnowBot numbers (Studio → Set up → SMS / Telephone → "Get your KnowBot number"): the customer picks a number in their
# area, pays in place (embedded checkout), and the number is bought on the Twilio account above and pointed at their bot.
# Price: $10/mo service + the number's monthly cost x 1.2, plus prepaid call/text credit packs ($10/$25/$50) drawn down
# at cost x 1.2 per call minute and per text segment. Off ("coming soon") unless STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN are all set. Use Recourse Software Inc's Stripe account (the one KnowDrive.ai uses).
# Prefer a restricted key (rk_…) with only: Checkout Sessions, Customers, Subscriptions, Refunds, Prices/Products (write).
STRIPE_RESTRICTED_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Signing secret of the webhook endpoint <public API origin>/api/studio/numbers/webhook (events: checkout.session.completed,
# checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded, customer.subscription.deleted). Without it, payments are still confirmed when
# the checkout completes in the Studio, but a closed tab is only caught up by the webhook.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Provider costs (USD) are read from the provider's pricing API; set these to fix them instead (used as-is, x 1.2).
# If the API can't be read and these are unset: 1.15 a month, 0.0085 a minute, 0.0083 a text.
# KNOWBOT_NUMBER_COST_MONTHLY=1.15
# KNOWBOT_NUMBER_COST_MINUTE=0.0085
# KNOWBOT_NUMBER_COST_TEXT=0.0083
# Gemini Live voice-to-voice phone calls (aistudio.google.com/apikey). Without it the phone line answers that it isn't set
# up yet and hangs up.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL=gemini-3.8-live
# GEMINI_VOICE=Kore
# The same key powers the web voice assistant (lib/voice-widget.js, embed data-mode="voice"); without it the widget uses
# the browser's own speech recognition and voice. Limits: KNOWBOT_WEBVOICE_MAX_SECONDS=600, KNOWBOT_WEBVOICE_MAX_SESSIONS=50,
# KNOWBOT_WEBVOICE_MAX_PER_BOT=10 (open sessions per bot), KNOWBOT_WEBVOICE_MAX_PER_IP=2 (open sessions per IP),
# KNOWBOT_WEBVOICE_RATE_LIMIT=6 (sessions per minute per IP).
# Phone call limits (each open call holds a Gemini Live session): KNOWBOT_PHONE_MAX_SECONDS=900 (goodbye + hang-up),
# KNOWBOT_PHONE_MAX_SESSIONS=50 open calls, KNOWBOT_PHONE_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_BOT=5. Texted links: KNOWBOT_PHONE_TEXTS_PER_NUMBER=3
# per destination per 24 h, KNOWBOT_PHONE_TEXTS_PER_DAY=100 per bot; only to the caller's own number or a number in the
# same country as TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER, never premium-rate or short codes.
# Texted checkout links use each bot's own Shopify store import (or a launched bot's shopDomain). For local development
# only, SHOP_DOMAIN applies to the ONE bot named by SHOP_DOMAIN_BOT (never server-wide).
# SHOP_DOMAIN=https://your-store.example
# SHOP_DOMAIN_BOT=front-desk

# "Send me this information": a visitor on any surface can ask the bot to send them its last answer (with sources and the
# proof link) by email or text. Email goes through Resend (resend.com, a verified knowbot.knowdrive.ai sending domain);
# without RESEND_API_KEY email is off and the bot offers a text instead. Texts use the Twilio settings above
# (TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID + TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN + TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER). Neither configured: the bot never offers to send.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# The sending address; the bot's name replaces the display name ("Waterdown Village Chiropractic <answers@…>").
# KNOWBOT_EMAIL_FROM=KnowBot <answers@knowbot.knowdrive.ai>
# Limits: KNOWBOT_SENDINFO_PER_CALLER_HOUR=5, KNOWBOT_SENDINFO_PER_DEST_HOUR=5, KNOWBOT_SENDINFO_PER_BOT_DAY=200.

# Evidence selector (attendd, a loopback sidecar in the container image). Off unless KNOWBOT_EVIDENCE=attend; when on and
# the sidecar answers, it picks the passages each answer may quote (replacing the search step); any error or timeout falls
# back to the search path. Local runs: scripts/fetch-engine.sh, then (cd attendd && go build) and run ./attendd/attendd.
# KNOWBOT_EVIDENCE=attend
# ATTENDD_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7071
# A weak match (the passages cover too little of the question) is the fixed refusal; =answer lets the answer step decide.
# KNOWBOT_EVIDENCE_WEAK=answer
